ny involves three parties: the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"authenticator"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (a YubiKey), the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"client","type":"text"}]},{"text":" (your app, via ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Client"},{"text":"), and the ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"relying party"}]},{"text":" (your server, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"verifies what the authenticator returns). The client is the communication path between","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"authenticator and relying party — and it verifies the relying party’s identity against","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the origin it’s bound to, so it can refuse to sign for a fraudulent site.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"There are two ceremonies. ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Registration"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Client\/makeCredential(_:authorization:)"},{"text":") creates a new credential and supplies its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"public key to the relying party for account association. ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Authentication"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Client\/getAssertion(_:authorization:)"},{"text":") proves to the relying party that the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"YubiKey is the one registered for the user. Both ceremonies follow the same mechanical","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shape: the relying party supplies a challenge, the authenticator signs it together"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the relying-party identifier, and the signature goes back to the relying party"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"for verification.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The pieces fit together as: a connection carries CTAP2 traffic, a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/CTAP2\/Session","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sits on top, and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/WebAuthn\/Client","type":"reference"},{"text":" runs ceremonies on that session. Connections come in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"three flavours that all work for WebAuthn: ","type":"text"},{"code":"YubiKit\/HIDFIDOConnection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on macOS,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/NFCSmartCardConnection","type":"reference"},{"text":" for tap-to-auth on iOS, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/yubikit-swift.YubiKit\/documentation\/YubiKit\/USBSmartCardConnection","type":"reference"},{"text":" on either platform. Pick the one that matches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"your platform and form factor.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ macOS — USB HID FIDO","let connection = try await HIDFIDOConnection()","\/\/ iOS — tap-to-auth over NFC:","\/\/ let connection = try await NFCSmartCardConnection()","","let session = try await CTAP2.Session.makeSession(connection: connection)","let client = WebAuthn.Client(","    session: session,","    origin: 